 "answer_html": "<h3>Definition</h3><p>Java can display images (JPG, PNG, GIF) by loading them with <b>ImageIO.read()</b> or <b>ImageIcon</b> and drawing them with <b>drawImage()</b>.</p><h3>Key points</h3><ul><li>Load: <code>Image img = ImageIO.read(new File(\"cat.jpg\"));</code></li><li>Draw in paintComponent: <code>g.drawImage(img, x, y, null);</code></li><li>Easy way: <code>new JLabel(new ImageIcon(\"cat.jpg\"))</code>.</li><li>Can scale: <code>g.drawImage(img, x, y, width, height, null)</code>.</li></ul>",
 "quiz": {
  "q": "Which method draws a picture?",
  "options": [
   "drawString()",
   "drawImage()",
   "setIcon()"
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "why": "Load Then Draw."
 }
